\n+++ b/docs/quality/records/CLOUD-EFFICIENCY-01.json\n@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@\n   \"purpose\": \"Reduce Cloud historical downloads and safely isolate exact prepared sources without lowering quality gates\",\n   \"player_experience\": \"Faster bounded engineering feedback preserves real game and human/device acceptance boundaries\",\n   \"constraints\": [\n-    \"All original check definitions, assertions, timeouts and profile prefixes retained\",\n+    \"All original check commands, assertions, timeouts and profile prefixes retained; add the actually read retained fixtures to original inputs\",\n     \"No core gameplay or historical evidence/resource deletion; no history rewrite\",\n     \"Missing, changed or corrupt required inputs fail; hydration is never test PASS\",\n     \"Existing policy classifies config/production_impact.json under production paths; use small_fix with formal_impact=false for this nonvisual routing metadata/tooling change instead of exempting it from the policy\"\n@@ -386,5 +386,5 @@\n     \"Exact final-SHA Integration CI pending at this checkpoint; use PR103 actual check status\",\n     \"Original main/manual complete Release and physical devices/player quality remain separate\"\n   ],\n-  \"test_change_justification\": \"Keep all 158 original check contracts and original profile prefixes. Append cloud-inputs-tests; preserve all existing test assertions. New real sparse/partial Git, deletion, corruption, transport and execution counterexamples. Finite formal-player/enemy Development paths retain full Integration and shared Bible guard. Exact-HEAD CI remains mandatory; original main/manual Release remains. Also append the unchanged existing portable frozen-asset test with its exact fixture directory so sparse CI restores the actual pre-export consumer dependency; its new registration has independent review and will run in complete docs/CI.\"\n+  \"test_change_justification\": \"Keep all 158 original check contracts and original profile prefixes. Append cloud-inputs-tests; preserve all existing test assertions. New real sparse/partial Git, deletion, corruption, transport and execution counterexamples. Finite formal-player/enemy Development paths retain full Integration and shared Bible guard. Exact-HEAD CI remains mandatory; original main/manual Release remains. Also append the unchanged existing portable frozen-asset test with its exact fixture directory so sparse CI restores the actual pre-export consumer dependency; its new registration has independent review and will run in complete docs/CI. CI83 exposed one undeclared historical fixture; finite read-only transitive audit identified five affected native checks. Extend their existing inputs (runtime roots when absent) only, retain all argv/assertions/success patterns/timeouts/serial flags and keep the actual failed run. Metadata is not a complete inferred graph.\"\n }",
